{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3959958","formula":"C₃₁H₅₂N₂O₂₃","hill":"C31H52N2O23","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":31.0,"H":52.0,"N":2.0,"O":23.0},"names":{"en":"Sialyl-Lewis X","ru":"CD15"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sialyl LewisX (sLeX), also known as cluster of differentiation 15s (CD15s) or stage-specific embryonic antigen 1 (SSEA-1), is a tetrasaccharide carbohydrate which is usually attached to O-glycans on the surface of cells. It is known to play a vital role in cell-to-cell recognition processes. It is also the means by which an egg attracts sperm; first, to stick to it, then bond with it and eventually form a zygote.","ru":"CD15 (3-фукозил-N-ацетиллактозамин, Lewis X) — углеводная молекула адгезии, производное дисахарида, иммунологически важная молекула, которая может быть компонентом гликопротеинов, гликолипидов и протеогликанов. В отличие от большинства молекул, относящихся к кластерам дифференцировки, которые являются белками, CD15 является углеводом."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":643990,"mass":820.7,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H]1[C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](O1)O[C@H]([C@H](C=O)NC(=O)C)[C@@H]([C@@H](CO)O)O[C@H]2[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H]([C@H](O2)CO)O)O[C@@]3(C[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H](O3)[C@@H]([C@@H](CO)O)O)NC(=O)C)O)C(=O)O)O)O)O)O","inchikey":"LAQPKDLYOBZWBT-NYLDSJSYSA-N","iupac":"(2S,4S,5R,6R)-5-acetamido-2-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[(2R,3R,4R,5R)-5-acetamido-1,2-dihydroxy-6-oxo-4-[(2S,3S,4R,5S,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxyhexan-3-yl]oxy-3,5-dihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-4-yl]oxy-4-hydroxy-6-[(1R,2R)-1,2,3-trihydroxypropyl]oxane-2-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"643990","atoms":108,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.097,"y":-2.947,"z":1.563,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.214,"y":-2.817,"z":0.049,"el":"C"},{"x